            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0816" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4R1/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Observer at the Conference on the
                        Suppression of Opium Smoking at Bangkok</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-09T15:00:00+07:00">November 9, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 9—6:43 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Conference was opened by Siamese Minister for Foreign Affairs and after
                    organization adjourned until tomorrow morning when statements of delegates are
                    invited.</p>
                <p>Siamese Under Secretary of State Foreign Affairs elected President, and Van
                    Wettum, Vice President.</p>
                <p>China not represented, ostensibly for financial reasons.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
